Package: taos-power
Version: 0.1.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: jaylfc <jaylfc25@gmail.com>
Priority: optional
Section: admin
Depends: systemd
Description: taOS power policy: a taOS machine does not sleep by default
 Provides the taos-power command. A taOS machine is a server (it serves models
 to phones and other devices), so the always-on profile, the default on any
 machine without a battery, never suspends or hibernates: it writes logind and
 sleep.conf drop-ins that ignore the power key, lid switch and idle action and
 disallow every sleep mode. The battery profile, the default when a battery is
 present, allows suspend and changes nothing. An optional, off by default CPU
 tune (taos-power tune performance) sets the performance governor and holds a
 low PM QoS wake-up latency request while the taos-power unit runs.
